  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Transportation secretary Sean Duffy blames prior presidents and Congress for flight stoppage",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/15/transportation-secretary-sean-duffy-faa-flight-stoppag",
      "description": "<p>Democratic senator Chris Van Hollen says Trump administration hasn’t properly invested existing funds</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration\">Donald Trump’s administration</a> on Sunday blamed the travel chaos stemming from Friday’s four-hour nationwide<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/14/faa-ground-stop-flights-resume-airport-chaos\"> flight stoppage</a> on prior presidents as well as a lack of congressional funding – though a Democratic senator argued that the Trump administration hasn’t properly invested all of the funds it has already been given to implement needed air travel infrastructure upgrades.</p><p>“I take responsibility for what was given to me by prior administrations,” the US transportation secretary, Sean Duffy, told CNN’s Dana Bash, a day after he said routine but necessary maintenance botched by a contractor had caused Friday’s Federal Aviation Administration (FAA)<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/13/faa-ground-stop-flights-explained\"> ground stop</a>, leading to the delay or cancellation of thousands of flights.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/15/transportation-secretary-sean-duffy-faa-flight-stoppag\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-15T16:18:49"
    },
    {
      "title": "Two planes collide on taxiway at Miami airport one day after national grounding",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/15/miami-airport-planes-collide",
      "description": "<p>Two people injured after wingtip of Copa Airlines Boeing 737 struck nose of United Parcel Service Boeing 767</p><p>Two planes collided with one another on a taxiway at Miami’s international airport on Saturday night – a day after the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) issued an hours-long nationwide ground stop <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/13/faa-ground-stop-flights-explained\">due</a> to communication issues affecting multiple air traffic control centers.</p><p>In a statement, the Trump administration-led <a href=\"https://www.faa.gov/newsroom/statements/accident_incidents\">FAA</a> said the wingtip of a Copa Airlines Boeing 737 struck the nose of a United Parcel Service Boeing 767 “while the airplanes were taxiing at Miami International Airport”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/15/miami-airport-planes-collide\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-15T15:40:04"
    },
    {
      "title": "Trump breaks silence about FAA nationwide ground stop, blames Biden administration",
